# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to the root of any project as `.envrc` (note the dot).
# Requires `direnv` installed + hooked into your shell, and the direnv
# extension enabled in VS Code (or `direnv allow` run once per project).
#
# With this in place, `cd`-ing into the project (or opening it in
# VS Code's integrated terminal) automatically loads the life-hub
# devShell — no manual `nix develop`, and nothing is installed
# globally or left behind when you leave the directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
use flake
